150, 21467160, 19336573). Experimental studies have revealed that truncating mutations promote cancer cell proliferation, survival and metastasis, since ectopic expression of these mutations in melanoma cells increased cell motility and tumor formation in vivo. This was due in part to aberrant localization of truncated proteins to the mitochondria, regulating genes involved in cell survival, including CypD (PMID: 27759562).	Tumor Suppressor	14	94	64	0	AG>A	1.71078683125754	0.254798038697932	5.65308453126359	0.559887709362822	5.65308453126359	0.87037037037037	1190180	2	0	2
